  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 946 PM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nA cold front associated with a deepening trough over the E U.S.\nwill move through the region Thursday. This will bring the best\nrain chances of the period along with highs held in the upper 80s\nto low 90s. Any stronger storms Thursday could produce gusty winds\nand heavy rainfall, through organized severe weather appears\nlimited. \n\nBehind the front, temperatures settle closer to seasonal normals\nFriday through the weekend, with highs generally in the upper 80s\nto low 90s and lower humidity. Additional chances of showers and \nstorms linger into the weekend as residual moisture and weak \ndisturbances rotate around the trough, but coverage should be more\nscattered. \n\nBy early next week, high pressure builds briefly, favoring\nmostly dry conditions and continued seasonable temperatures.\nConfidence is good in the overall cooling and increased\nprecipitation trend through the weekend. \n\nThe prolonged heat episode of mid-August is effectively ending.\nEnjoy the more comfortable conditions Thursday, then prepare for a\nwetter stretch through the end of next week.",
